{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/812707-story-help","id":812707,"title":"story help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-20T10:25:50-08:00","id":812707,"title":"story help","content":"I\u2019m trying to work with my group to have each ghost wolf have a story line so they don\u2019t just join for the sake of the game. What are some good ideas for trying to get two or three ghost wolves to join one another? Any other starter ideas will be much appreciated as well and not just for were wolf the forsaken<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11063-dalurain","name":"dalurain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:20:28-08:00","id":812744,"title":"","content":"Did all your players want to be Ghost Wolves or is that a story requirement? Finding tribal mentors could make for a great motivation. Your players Aspirations will also give you clues what kinds of stories that they want.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, even Ghost Wolves, have the packing instinct. I'd suggest you start them off with a common threat, a spirit or powerful claimed hunting them, and alone any one of them is easy meat. Start in the middle of the action too: it's more dramatic to begin with &quot;Your characters lean against whatever is nearby for support, catching ragged breaths through searing lungs. What was that thing and why did it want to kill you? Worse yet... how far away was it? You hear birds take flight from their night roosts as something startles them awake and know it won't be long before it finds you again... what do you do?&quot; in comparison to &quot;You're all in the same restaurant, sitting apart from one another, checking your smart phones. What do you do?&quot;<br /> <br /> Especially in the first story or until your players get used to the system, provide a lot of direction. Flat out make them have character ties to each other as part of creation. They don't need to be friends... imagine a new pack based off the stereotype of three high school students (the jock, the nerd, and the preppy girl) who change at nearly the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:43:01-08:00","id":812762,"title":"","content":"My idea was that all of them are indeed ghost wolves. I do like the idea of a mentor but what if it was a hunter who has passed his prime and seen not all things that have gone bump in the night are evil. As for the high school idea or common ties I get it. Perhaps after they get themselves out of whatever the danger is then they tell each other why they were there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11063-dalurain","name":"dalurain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:58:36-08:00","id":812768,"title":"","content":"Inciting incidents can be difficult, especially if you are trying to smooth the contrived &quot;party-up&quot; convention prevalent in table top games. I ended up starting my first crossover game with a SAW parody (Characters all awoke in a bizarre, extraspacial torture dungeon belonging megalomaniac who sought to educate them on their monstrous nature. They proceed to bulldoze all the 'tests' and maul the pathetic psychopath. A good bonding experience for all.) to avoid that issue<br /> <br /> Some ideas I've thought of:<ul><li>All characters begin in jail, arrested for assorted crimes, and escape in the same mass jailbreak. They stick together because dammit, someone has to have their back.</li> <li>A mysterious outsider (possibly mentor) manipulates the characters together to serve his own ends. A mysterious phone call, email or letter to each, that draws them together at a time convenient to the manipulator's ends. The characters survive and ban together either with or against their mysterious summoner.</li> <li>A volcano has emerged in the shadow, there's no explaining why or how, but it's got all the local spirits in a tizzy, attacking the Forsaken with reckless abandon. Ghost wolves find themselves all driven to the same, high gauntlet density area for personal safety (could substitute in a mentor's protected safe-house).</li> <li>A new pack of Pure are in town, looking to hammer out a territory. They are willing to 'recruit' Forsaken, and respond brutally to anyone who rejects their generous offer. Ghost wolves are forced to ban together or else be slaughtered by the more organized predators (you can do the same with any hunter group, sans the recruitment bit).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}